<!-- THIS FILE IS THE EDITABLE SOURCE (a `.tmpl`, not itself a served page) --
     a generic starting point, same convention as site/privacy.html.tmpl.example.
     Copy it to site/index_embedded.html.tmpl (untracked, never overwritten by
     an upgrade -- see README.md "Static-site pages"), replace every
     REPLACE-ME marker and the course list below, then let `my-bt setup -i`
     (or scripts/render-site.py at build time) render it into the real,
     served site/index_embedded.html -- same real-or-.example resolution,
     and the same generated/never-hand-edited relationship between the two,
     as site/privacy.html.tmpl -> site/privacy.html.

     What this file is for: a no-JavaScript variant of site/index.html.example,
     meant specifically for embedding this site via <iframe> on another,
     separate site (2026-07-XX: added after a visitor got a security alert
     opening a page that embeds this site in an <iframe> -- the regular
     index.html's two <script> blocks make same-origin fetch() calls that,
     from INSIDE a third-party iframe, look like tracking behavior to
     privacy-conscious browsers/extensions, which can block the iframe's
     content outright rather than just the cookie). This page has NO
     <script> tags at all, so there's nothing for a script/tracker blocker,
     or a Content-Security-Policy script-src mismatch, to ever catch --
     see README.md "Static-site pages" for the full reasoning and the
     regular index.html's own equivalent commentary.

     Two direct consequences of having no JS:
     - The Login button is plain, static HTML -- always just "Login", never
       session-aware (no swap to "My bookings"/"Log out" the way the
       regular index.html opportunistically does, since that swap needs a
       live fetch()). Simpler, and correct: a session-aware swap wouldn't
       reliably work from inside a third-party iframe anyway (modern
       browsers increasingly block/partition third-party cookies), so
       nothing of real value is lost by not attempting it here.
     - The `$${schedule_exceptions_html}` placeholder below is filled in
       AS PART OF THE RENDER STEP, not fetched live in the visitor's
       browser -- `my-bt setup -i`/scripts/render-site.py bakes in whatever
       upcoming [[course.date_override]] entries settings.toml currently
       has at the moment this file is (re)generated. This means the
       exceptions shown here can go stale if settings.toml changes and this
       page is never regenerated -- see app/cli_checks.py::
       check_index_embedded_drift, which is exactly the check that catches
       that gap (`my-bt status`/`setup`/`setup -i` all report it).

     Every link meant to be clicked from inside the embedding iframe (Login,
     every course's booking link, and the footer's legal-page links) uses
     target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" -- opens in a NEW tab rather
     than trying (and failing, or looking broken/tiny) to load inside the
     small embedded iframe, and rel="noopener noreferrer" is the plain-HTML
     defense against the new tab getting a `window.opener` handle back to
     the embedding page. Keep this on every outbound link if you add more --
     an easy thing to forget on a new link (the regular index.html.example
     itself used to only have this on the Login link, not the course
     booking links, which was a real gap since embedded booking links would
     otherwise try to open inside the tiny iframe too). -->
<html>
<head>
<meta http-equiv=Content-Type content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
<title>REPLACE-ME-YOUR-SITE-NAME</title>
<style>
 body { max-width: 760px; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; font-family: sans-serif; }
 footer { margin-top: 3em; font-size: 0.85em; color: #666; }
 .top-bar { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
 .login-btn { font-size: 0.85em; padding: 0.3em 0.9em; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 4px;
              text-decoration: none; color: #222; }
 .login-btn:hover { background: #f4f7f4; }
 .attention { background: #fdecea; border: 1px solid #f5c2c0; border-radius: 8px;
              padding: 0.8em 1.2em; margin: 0.6em 0; color: #a61b1b; }
 .attention a { color: #a61b1b; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="top-bar"><a class="login-btn" href="/my" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Login</a></div>

${schedule_exceptions_html}

<h1>REPLACE-ME-YOUR-SITE-NAME</h1>

<p>REPLACE-ME: a short description of what you offer and who it's for.</p>

<h2>Upcoming sessions</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/book/example-monday-class" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Example Class -- Monday 18:00: book your place here.</a></li>
  <li><a href="/book/example-thursday-class" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Example Class (Advanced) -- Thursday 19:00: book your place here.</a></li>
</ul>

<footer>
<a href="/terms.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
<a href="/privacy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy policy</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
<a href="/impressum.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Impressum / Legal notice</a>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
